Say what?  That's not the issue at all.

The core issue is that shopkeepers are yelling specific things about the
player (race) when they haven't seen/can't see the player.

The ideal solution: shopkeepers come to the door so their line of sight
is sufficient to see the player from a number of areas.

The problem with that: shopkeepers are 'smart' and will tend to stay out
of line with the player so they can't be easily hit by wands.  This
behavior is good, because it generally will force the player to go
_inside_ the shop to fight at range with the shopkeeper -- leaving the
player with nowhere to run if the fight goes poorly.

Forcing the shopkeeper to come to the door puts him at much greater risk
than he would normally put himself, and allows the player to take
potshots at the keeper from a much greater range -- and most
importantly, with an available escape route.

