Just because they're largely ineffective doesn't mean that they should
be removed completely.  They _can_ serve as a deterrent, after all; it's
just that the player, being controlled by a human _and_ having far more
resources than any shopkeeper, will naturally have the edge in any ranged duel.

Wands are far more effective in circumstances where the player _doesn't_
have plenty of time to prepare; shopkeepers start out peaceful, so the
player can get all his ducks in a row prior to engaging in combat.

(Crossbows would be significantly less useful than wands.)

